[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "89dc9b84-e2ee-53df-b6b2-c379048ba671",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-4 \\\\ x+2y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-4,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8bff99ce-0a16-5ff2-98d7-78ce1c63ad65",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
