    "question": {
      ":question/id": "32413134-e7e7-53f5-bbe0-847237a55e86",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=2 \\\\ x+2y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "869be4a1-6b7e-5f7f-aaaf-3b2c935341a0",
