    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "791cfbde-2944-5c8b-9622-451cad73ac8d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=-3 \\\\ -x+y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=1,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "2d3747a1-afe8-54db-a96b-43f318545cb2",
